The baseline is already a single ciphertext addition, which is the minimum for this function. The output depends on both inputs, so at least one operation is required. I can't remove any operation, and any rewrite would either keep the same circuit or add work. I'm therefore resubmitting the minimal kernel unchanged.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x0("x0");
  Ciphertext x1("x1");
  Ciphertext y = x0 + x1;
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

The circuit is already a single ciphertext add, so no cheaper circuit exists. Any structurally different version would add operations, because the output needs both inputs and there is no way to combine them with fewer than one operation. Alternatives like `x0 - (-x1)` or `(x0 + x1)` routed through extra ops only add cost. I'm keeping the minimal kernel, since a different circuit can't be faster here.

